A||N||12||Monkeyman||Got another Fiero!!||||10||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||12-25-2000||10:27 PM||||I just got my Christmas present last night.  An '85 GT.  Oooh!  99% stock and only 71,399 miles.  Previously owned by a perfectionist.  What more can I ask for?  Other than a few minor problems (headlights won't completely retract (time for those non pop ups?? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">), desperately needs a new alternator belt, one front marker light has a short and the sail panels are damaged), it's damn near perfect.  Best of all, it's a stick.  I just realized that there's nothing like owning/driving a stick shift Fiero GT.  (Well...nothing I can mention on a family forum. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">)  The new GT corners better than my current ride (another '85 GT, of course) and is smoother, too.  Go figure.  A little bit of work on the above mentioned problems (no big deal) and this thing will be perfect.  Other than a couple of very small tears in the drivers bolster, the interior is a 9.99999.  I swapped steering wheels with the one in the Grape Ape today (aftermarket) and installed Rodneys short/sport shifter.  This week, modifications, etc will include a trip to the shop to replace the alt belt, swap rims/tires with the Grape Ape, and the start of my stereo installation (head unit and component speakers 1st--amp as soon as my friend gets back to work and helps me make an enclosure for it).  I'll try to take some pics as I go. <P>Sorry for the bandwidth, but I couldn't contain myself any longer. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000001||Oreif||12-25-2000||10:36 PM||||Congrats Monkeyman! What are you going to do with the "Grape Ape" now? What do we call the new one? What color is it? Details, we need more details.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000002||MooCow||12-25-2000||11:50 PM||||I would like to see pics of this new GT you have.  Congrats on your new Fiero. Don't go and drive it in this weather.  I wouldn't want that pretty GT getting smashed up so be carefull.<P>                               Thanks Ken ||||reg||10
Z||000003||Standard||12-26-2000||03:20 AM||||<B>sweeeeet</B>!!!  Let's see some pics!!!<P>------------------<BR>Mike -<BR>Black 86.5 GT 5 Spd, 153,000 miles and some busted up ground f/x  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/redface.gif"> <BR>Red 84 Sport Coupe - winter donut maker    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/asthanos.gif"> ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Monkeyman||12-26-2000||04:47 AM||||Pics soon.  I'm keeping the Grape Ape through spring at least.  I'll drive the new GT as much as the weather will allow, but if it gets too bad, I'll drive the Grape Ape.  Every time I think I know exactly what color I want to paint the new GT, I seem to change my mind.  It's currently factory red with the standard gray/silver ground fx.  I was originally planning on a gunmetal gray/black scheme, but it will cost the same to repaint it in almost any color (around 3 grand last I checked--OUCH!).  I love the color of the Grape Ape (pearlized purple for those that haven't seen it) so I might just paint the new GT the same color.  Since it'll cost so much to repaint, it'll be a while before I can afford to do so.  I need to pick a name for this one, but since I'm not sure of the color change yet, it needs to be one that is independant of the color.  Any suggestions?||||reg||1
Z||000005||hugh||12-26-2000||07:34 AM||||How about KONG for when you repower it(you know you will)?||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phil||12-26-2000||08:19 AM||||Grand Simian then you'll have a GS GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||Coconut||12-26-2000||01:18 PM||||MM,<BR>Now that is some really great news! I was all bummed to hear of your predicament with the Monkeymobile in storage but I guess that this may somewhat ease a little pain of having to lose it. Great score partner! I'm happy for ya!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>As far as a name for the GT....hows about "Mighty Joe" (after Mighty Joe Young) being that its a GT and all!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Cruisin' On,  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Coconut's_Signature_1.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by Coconut (edited 12-26-2000).]||||reg||14
